# Task: review concerns

The owner wants to focus on problems and loose ends. Find them, rank them, and work
through them one at a time. Hidden records are problems too, so every query includes them
(`includeHidden: true`).

## Steps

1. Gather the evidence with `{{ tools.query }}`:

```graphql
query Concerns {
  reviews(includeHidden: true) { id note target { collection id field entity { __typename } } }
  activeVersion { modified basedOn { number tag } }
  staff(includeHidden: true) { id name hidden photo { id } }
  services(includeHidden: true) { id name hidden image { id } }
  unusedAssets: assets(unused: true, includeHidden: true) { id type path }
  unregisteredFiles: resourceFiles(unregistered: true)
  trash { ref { collection id } label deletedAt }
}
```

2. Build a **concerns table** (priority, concern, affected records), covering:
   - open review items: questions the owner has to answer;
   - staff without a photo and services without an image;
   - uploaded images that are not used by any record (hidden or not), and uploaded files
     not registered as assets;
   - hidden records: confirm they should stay off the website;
   - records in the trash: restore or leave for purging;
   - unsaved changes since the last snapshot (`modified`).
3. Take the concerns one at a time, highest priority first: explain it, propose a fix
   (the query or mutation you would run), and ask the owner. Make changes only through
   `{{ tools.mutate }}`, after the owner agrees, as in the `update_business` prompt.
4. After each fix, show what changed, then move to the next concern.

